From 5930568b2f15c649d2b342fba2ec614ab63174d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zczyh0922 <345248607+zczyh0922@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:13:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi/phy: 7nm: program the PLL muxes on every bias
 enable

Since "drm/msm: dsi: fix PLL init in bonded mode" was reverted,
dsi_7nm_phy_enable() takes the PLL bias reference itself by setting
pll_enable_cnt to 1, without programming PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES. Every later
dsi_pll_enable_pll_bias() call then returns early and skips the mux
write and its settle delay. A rate read-back or rate change before the
PHY enable drops the reference back to zero on its way out, and that
disable path clears PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES, so nothing restores the mux.

On the bonded dual-DSI panel of the OnePlus Pad 2 Pro this left the
internal display dark, or the half driven by the secondary link
garbled, depending on the probe order; the touch controller integrated
in the panel then reported checksum errors. Both reports came from
units running ColorOS C.35.

Keep the reference counting, the lock and the power-down path, set
PLL_SHUTDOWNB only when the first reference is taken, and write the mux
and wait 250 ns on every call.

Adapted from the patch posted in the issue below; only the comment
wording differs.

Fixes: 44784327815b ("Revert \"drm/msm: dsi: fix PLL init in bonded mode\"")
Link: https://github.com/yzddmr6/onepluspad-2pro-mainline/issues/14
Link: https://github.com/yzddmr6/onepluspad-2pro-mainline/issues/13
Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c | 14 ++++++--------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
index 5d805a797..04f315c71 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
@@ -426,16 +426,14 @@ static void dsi_pll_enable_pll_bias(struct dsi_pll_7nm *pll)
 	u32 data;
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&pll->pll_enable_lock, flags);
-	if (pll->pll_enable_cnt++) {
-		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pll->pll_enable_lock, flags);
-		WARN_ON(pll->pll_enable_cnt == INT_MAX);
-		return;
+	if (!pll->pll_enable_cnt++) {
+		data = readl(pll->phy->base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
+		data |= DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0_PLL_SHUTDOWNB;
+		writel(data, pll->phy->base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
 	}
+	WARN_ON(pll->pll_enable_cnt == INT_MAX);
 
-	data = readl(pll->phy->base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
-	data |= DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0_PLL_SHUTDOWNB;
-	writel(data, pll->phy->base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
-
+	/* dsi_7nm_phy_enable() takes the first reference without programming the muxes. */
 	writel(0xc0, pll->phy->pll_base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pll->pll_enable_lock, flags);
 	ndelay(250);
-- 
